GS: texture packs in PCSX2's format (GOW_TEXTURE_PACK=<folder>, GOW_TEXTURE_PACK_MB, the launcher's texture pack option). Each uploaded texture a draw samples gets the name PCSX2 gives its replacement (XXH3-64 of its GS memory blocks or unswizzled rows, XXH3-64 of the 32-bit palette, PSM/TW/TH/TEXA bits; xxHash v0.8.3 header through FetchContent); a PNG of that name in the pack replaces it, sampled as a direct-colour texture at its own resolution with mipmaps. PNGs are decoded on a worker thread (the game's texture is drawn until one is ready), uploaded by the render thread, and kept within a GPU memory budget (least recently used out first). GOW_TEX_PCSX2_NAMES=<file> lists the names of the textures drawn (to make or check packs). Combat on the ship with a PCSX2 pack: 81 images applied, 73 MB, no visible hitch; FPS within run-to-run noise.

